# Paths the code index must not ingest, one pattern per line; '#' comments out.
#
# benchmarks/results/ holds measurement evidence. Letting the index read it back
# would let the benchmark change the corpus it measures: indexing a single 6 KB
# baseline file cost 1.9pp of mean recall and one target-met task, because a
# derived file competed with source fragments for the same token budget.
benchmarks/results/

# Scratch space. Files under _tmp/ are working residue, not project source: a
# stray memory record dropped there on 2026-10-06 sat one index refresh away
# from competing for the same token budget (.json is an indexed suffix).
_tmp/

# Archify diagram workspaces and delivered diagrams are derived artifacts, and
# both .json and .html are indexed suffixes. A rendered diagram is one large
# inline-SVG file, so leaving it in the tree would let a generated picture
# outrank real source for the same budget - the same defect benchmarks/results/
# is excluded for.
.archify/
docs/architecture/

# The final report is a *measurement product*: a summary of numbers produced by
# the benchmark, restating them in prose with many identifiers. Leaving it in the
# corpus would let the write-up of the measurements compete with the code the
# measurements are about - the same rule benchmarks/results/ follows. Measured
# on 2026-10-15: adding it moved hinted recall by 2.5pp.
docs/final-report.md
